list.item:
Pate, Lieutenant General Randolph M., Assistant
                        Commandant of the Marine Corps and Chief of Staff until January 1, 1956;
                        thereafter Commandant

person.note:
Republican Senator from California; Senate Majority Leader until January 1955;
                    thereafter Senate Minority Leader; Member, Senate Foreign Relations Committee;
                    Member, Joint Committee on Atomic Energy

Assistant Secretary of Defense for Research and Development until August 1955;
                    Secretary of the Air Force, August 1955–April 1957; thereafter Deputy Secretary
                    of Defense

Chairman, General Advisory Committee, Atomic Energy Commission, until 1957;
                    Member, Science Advisory Committee, Office of Defense Mobilization, 1955–1956;
                    thereafter Chairman; Representative to Negotiations for the Establishment of the
                    International Atomic Energy Agency from August 1955

Commanding General, U.S. Army Forces, Far East, and Eighth U.S. Army, until
                    March 1955; Commander in Chief, Far East Command, April 1955–June 1955;
                    thereafter Chief of Staff, U.S. Army
